{"resourceIdentifier":"4708","resourceName":"Tasar Forest Carbon Project","description":"This Tasar Forest Carbon Project will promote tree-based wild silk production outside traditional forests by utilizing privately owned barren / fallow uplands of tribal farmers. The project will undertake wild silk (locally called Tasar) tree planting and promote sericulture-based livelihoods. Sericulture is a traditional livelihood, however lack of availability of host trees in natural forests constrains its expansion. Traditionally, the tribal communities in the targeted areas depend majorly on forests for their livelihoods and have a long history of wild silk production from natural forests – wild silk is second to agriculture as a source of livelihoods. However, production from the forests declined due to government regulation of forest access rights. Yet there are large areas in these regions that are severely degraded, fallow, etc. that would benefit from restoring their productive capacity and biodiversity through profitable tree planting investments. \r\nThe project is implemented by Cognisphere Solutions Ltd. (CSL) with investment from Climate Partner Impact GmbH starting in 2022. The project will afforest 2,000 hectares of privately-owned wastelands with Tasar silk-host trees in the adjoining states of Jharkhand and West Bengal in India. The project implementation started from May 2022 and plantations were initiated in the season Jun to Oct 2022.\r\nIt will involve the participation of ~3,000 households in 125 villages, grouped into two clusters broadly in Jharkhand, and West Bengal. People in the project areas are majorly tribals with limited options to escape poverty and deprivation. Tasar host trees such as Terminalia arjuna and T. tomentosa will form the core species, accompanied with a diversity of other indigenous tree species. The planted trees will be managed as long-term agroforestry systems –integrating crop production (intercropping), Tasar silk production and associated value chain development.","location":{"latitude":23.344315,"longitude":85.296013},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-10-30","endExclusive":"2023-11-30","endInclusive":"2023-11-29"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4708"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"COGNISPHERE SOLUTIONS LIMITED"},{"type":"string","value":"DELHI, India"},{"type":"string","value":"+91-9717164894"},{"type":"string","value":"satya@cognisphere.in"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"43299"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ARR"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AR-ACM0003"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2000 Hectares"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Earthood Services Limited"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"16/04/2026"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 01/09/2022 - 31/08/2042"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=100571&IDKEY=78723kjnf7kjandsaslmdv09887vaksmrmnwqkjoiuanfnfuq09138687409","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"VCS_PROJ_DESC_DRAFT_4708_26JUN2023.pdf","uploadDate":"2023-10-19T13:39:37.723Z"},{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=100180&IDKEY=hlksjoiuwqowrnoiuomnckjashoufifmln902309ksdflku098s138148220","documentType":"Listing Representation